++### Perplexity metric is broken — mean_nll ≈ 404, perplexity ≈ 1e175 (BUG)
++`held_out_perplexity` and `community_pack_perplexity` report absurd values on
++every evaluated model (e.g. `runs/20260701_170411` doc_causal simplewiki:
++`mean_nll=403.9`, `perplexity=2.56e175`). A per-token mean NLL is bounded by
++`ln(vocab)=ln(50257)≈10.8`, so ~404 is ~40× over the theoretical max — the
++aggregate is summing where it should be averaging, or the per-doc `mean_nll`
++from `eval/scoring.py:score_doc` is malformed for these checkpoints. Chase it
++down:
++- `eval/perplexity.py:179` does `mean_nll = np.mean(nll_list)`; each entry is
++  `score_doc(...)["mean_nll"]`, which at `eval/scoring.py:163` is
++  `nll_per_tok.mean()`. That mean() *should* be per-token. Verify the slice at
++  scoring.py:160-162 (`log_probs[logit_indices]` gather) isn't off — e.g.
++  scoring padding/`prefix_len` bookkeeping producing gigantic NLL on a few docs
++  that then dominate the mean, or `forward_inference` logits on the wrong scale.
++- Check whether it's a few catastrophic-NLL docs (truncated packs, EOS layout
++  mismatch) vs. uniformly ~404 across all docs (points at a scale/normalization
++  bug). Log the per-doc nll_list distribution.
++- MC-accuracy CIs are fine and trustworthy; ONLY the perplexity path is bad.
++  Until fixed, ignore every `*_perplexity` number in `eval_results.json`.
