++### 8-GPU (multi-rank DDP) training hangs — ROOT-CAUSED & FIXED 2026-06-17
++**Root cause:** `PackBatchSampler._apply_pack_truncation` did not enforce
++`token_budget` as a hard cap. Its `else` branch (when `effective_len < overshoot
++< prefix+body+suffix`) skipped the doc and let `overshoot` leak, so a pack made
++of many docs each carrying a non-trimmable prefix (the `*_prefix` layouts) could
++ship ABOVE `max_seq_len`. One oversized pack (observed: 10185 > 8192) trips the
++RoPE cos/sin cache assert (`cos.size(0) >= seq_len`) in the attention forward on
++whichever DDP rank drew it; that AssertionError unwinds into the end-of-run
++`ReproducibilityManager.__exit__` barrier, which hangs because the other ranks
++never reach it — masking the traceback and presenting as a generic collective
++hang. Manifests only at world_size ≥ 2 (a single GPU just raises visibly).
++
++**Fix:** `_apply_pack_truncation` now trims layout decoration (prefix/suffix) as
++a last resort — via the new `DocPlacement.decoration_trim` field, honored in
++`data/collate.py` (drops suffix first, then prefix tail, preserving the prefix
++card's leading marker) — so the pack hits `token_budget` EXACTLY: the doc is
++kept, its body preserved as far as possible, no under-fill, never over budget.
++`decoration_trim` is also persisted through `epoch_precompute.PackRecord` so the
++precomputed/bucketed path stays consistent. Regression tests:
++`tests/data/test_pack_sampler.py::test_pack_truncation_is_a_hard_cap_with_prefixes`
++(+ `_no_overshoot_is_noop`). Verified end-to-end (job 42247, 4-GPU arxiv smoke):
++blew past the old gstep-76 crash, all ranks max seqlen = 8191.
++
++How it was diagnosed (the prior blocker — rank-0-only logs): added opt-in
++`TS2TS_DEBUG=1` per-rank file logging + `faulthandler` watchdog
++(`debug_instrumentation.py`) and a try/except around `smart_train` in `main.py`
++that logs the per-rank traceback before the masking barrier.
++
++### Per-rank Triton-kernel autotune stall at ≥2 ranks (BUG — separate, still open)
++After the truncation fix, the same smoke run stalled at gstep≈110: one rank
++(GPU idle, 0% util) sat in the **custom Triton kernel's autotuner** — the saved
++stack is `kernels/cross_doc_bitmask_bim_v18.py:forward` →
++`triton.runtime.autotuner.do_bench` → `triton.compiler.compile` / `make_llir`
++(NOT FlexAttention; training uses `triton_v18`). The `cdb_bim_v18` kernel
++autotunes per input shape, so a mask/grant shape first seen by one rank triggers
++a fresh JIT-compile+benchmark of all autotune configs ONLY on that rank, while
++the peers busy-wait (100% util) at the next gradient all-reduce. Each rank also
++has its OWN inductor/triton cache (`launch_slurm.py:70` →
++`/tmp/torchinductor_<job>/rank<N>`), so nothing is shared. The autotune appeared
++to hang (>10 min) — needs confirmation whether it's pathological autotune time or
++a true livelock. Candidate fixes: persist/share the Triton autotune cache across
++ranks, pre-warm the kernel on representative shapes before the loop, pin/reduce
++the autotune config space for v18, or pad grant/mask tensors to rank-invariant
++shapes. Reproduce with `TS2TS_DEBUG=1` and watch `nvidia-smi` for one idle GPU
++while others are pinned; confirm the stall frame is the v18 autotuner.
++
++### Live PackedSequenceDataset: dedup docs within an epoch (TODO — consider)
++The live `PackedSequenceDataset` / `PackBatchSampler` path samples WITH
++replacement: seeds are drawn via `self._rng.randrange(num_nodes)` and dedup is
++only *within* a pack (`pack_doc_ids`), with no cross-pack/epoch visited set. So a
