++The arXiv graph is built from [unarXive 2024](https://huggingface.co/datasets/ines-besrour/unarxive_2024): papers are nodes and an in-text citation is an edge **when the cited paper is also in the corpus**. The link target the model learns to emit is the cited paper's **title** (`\cite{Some Paper Title}`), not an opaque id — so it is predictable at inference. Citations resolve to an in-corpus arXiv id via the unarXive bibliography (direct arXiv ids, ~14.5%) plus an OpenAlex-id→arXiv-id map built from the OpenAlex snapshot (recovering ~52% more, non-hub lateral edges); bodies are rehydrated to faithful LaTeX (display math inlined as `$…$`). Mean out-degree 4.3, one ~1.3M-node connected component. See `data/arxiv_graph_extractor/`.
